<p>Scottish police charged an Iranian man and a Romanian woman after they tried to enter HM Naval Base Clyde in Scotland on March 20, according to police statements reported across the three outlets. Britain’s nuclear-armed submarines are based there. Officials said the pair walked up to the gate and asked to be let in. Police later arrested the man under the UK’s National Security Act, while the woman was charged with breach of the peace. The incident drew attention because the site is one of the UK’s most sensitive military facilities and home to the country’s nuclear submarine fleet. Authorities said there was no wider danger to the public, and the swift response suggested the base’s security systems worked as intended, even as the case now moves to the courts.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/oQU7JTKplYkcmo2xeO8wolmLeeIL3N-nqdvtL0P1CyPeJU34ujGnrOIsSdEEq0EfmgXDz9uyAbGRm1p6ej-LyC_PlPQJM_aH0j9Ja7xAqd1bcyqZ9Zpjlvmb2Y4zq6mtb62aqWkwCakiMacimCzJngAWCy_UZgNC_1HA5PNkplynHCRqBLGPH9hNFRczK-VJ2UJwBuEdMqrHM0pP2QZVPUVXucm5bY8RpSl05lObSG6pMNSU3Ak' alt='One of Britain’s nuclear-powered submarines undergoing maintenance at H.M. Naval Base Clyde in Scotland in 2023.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Court appearance: Local reporting said both suspects are due to appear at Dumbarton Sheriff Court after charges were filed following the attempted entry.</li><li>Naming: Reports commonly refer to the same installation as both HM Naval Base Clyde and Faslane, a name taken from the nearby area on Scotland’s west coast.</li><li>Scottish public-order charge: In Scotland, breach of the peace is a broad offense used for conduct alleged to have caused alarm or serious disturbance, so it follows a different legal route from the National Security Act count used against the man.</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/21/world/europe/iran-scotland-naval-base-clyde.html'>Iranian Man Arrested After Trying to Enter U.K. Naval Base, Police Say</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/iranian-romanian-charged-after-enter-uks-nuclear-submarine-131280039'>Iranian and Romanian charged after trying to enter UK&#x27;s nuclear submarine base</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/iranian-man-romanian-woman-charged-over-attempt-to-enter-uk-submarine-base'>Iranian man, Romanian woman charged over attempt to enter UK submarine base</a> - straitstimes.com</li></ul>